---
const controls = [
  {
    title: "Reviewing Key Product Details",
    text: "Before production starts, we try to confirm key details such as dimensions, stone selection, finish direction, visible faces, and other product-specific requirements."
  },
  {
    title: "Connecting Material Choice",
    text: "Different stone types suit different applications. We help review material options based on the product type, intended use, finish expectations, and fabrication practicality."
  },
  {
    title: "Reducing Misalignment",
    text: "We try to confirm scope, quantity basis, finish assumptions, and visible details early so quotation expectations stay aligned with production requirements."
  },
  {
    title: "Paying Attention To Finishing",
    text: "For finished stone products, appearance matters as much as size. We pay attention to finish quality, visible surfaces, edge details, and overall presentation."
  },
  {
    title: "Supporting Protective Packing",
    text: "Stone products need protective export packing. We pay close attention to crate planning, shipment protection, and practical packing requirements for overseas delivery."
  },
  {
    title: "Following Orders",
    text: "We try to follow custom and project orders with closer attention to confirmed details, communication clarity, and the points that most often affect delivery outcomes."
  }
];

const risks = [
  "Stone selection or veining not matching expectations",
  "Finish direction or visible surface details not fully aligned",
  "Dimensions, edge details, or order scope confirmed too late",
  "Packing not strong enough for fragile export shipments",
  "Quotation assumptions not matching final production requirements"
];
---

<section class="quality-risk-control section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="why-section-heading">
      <h2>Quality Control And Risk Reduction</h2>
      <p>
        For overseas buyers, quality is not only about the finished product.
        We try to reduce these risks through clearer review, closer production
        coordination, and practical export awareness.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="quality-risk-control__layout">
      <div class="quality-risk-control__grid">
        {controls.map((item) => (
          <article class="quality-risk-control__card">
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.text}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>

      <aside class="quality-risk-control__panel">
        <div class="quality-risk-control__panel-box">
          <h3>Common Risks Buyers Want To Avoid</h3>

          <ul class="quality-risk-control__risk-list">
            {risks.map((risk) => (
              <li>{risk}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>

          <p class="quality-risk-control__panel-note">
            Our goal is not to promise perfection in every case, but to reduce
            avoidable mistakes by clarifying important details earlier and
            paying closer attention to the points that most often affect custom
            stone orders.
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>